# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Temple of the Eye" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	An Eye for a Favour
0	section	Talking to Wizard Persten
1	line	Wizard Persten	Hello!
1	line	Player	Hey there.
1	option	Who are you?
2	line	Player	Who are you?
2	line	Wizard Persten	What? You haven't heard of me? The great Mia Persten of the Order of Wizards? The leading researcher in teleportation magic? The creator of the Home Teleport spell?
2	line	Player	Oh, I'm sorry. I didn't mean to offend you. I'm {player}.
2	line	Wizard Persten	No offence taken! My research tends to take me far from the Wizards' Tower. I've been all across Gielinor and even to some other planes of existence!
2	line	Player	Other planes of existence? Sounds exciting!
2	line	Wizard Persten	Exciting and terrifying! Brilliant, right?
2	option	So what are you doing in Al Kharid?
3	action	below
2	option	See you around.
3	action	below
1	option	What's a wizard doing in Al Kharid?
2	cond	If the player already asked "Who are you?":
3	line	Player	So what are you doing in Al Kharid?
3	line	Wizard Persten	Should I not be in Al Kharid?
3	line	Player	Er... good question. I guess I just haven't seen a wizard around here before.
3	line	Wizard Persten	Well, maybe you should start expecting the unexpected! That way you can spend less time worrying about why I'm here, and more time asking life's real questions.
3	action	continues
2	cond	If the player did not ask "Who are you?":
3	line	Player	What's a wizard doing in Al Kharid?
3	line	Wizard Persten	Why shouldn't a wizard be in Al Kharid?
3	line	Player	Er... good question. I guess I just haven't seen a wizard around here before.
3	line	Wizard Persten	Well for a start, I'm not just any wizard. The name's Mia Persten. I'm the leading researcher in teleportation magic for the Order of Wizards.
3	line	Player	Pleased to meet you. I'm {player}.
3	line	Wizard Persten	Now as for your question, maybe you should start expecting the unexpected! That way you can spend less time worrying about why I'm here, and more time asking life's real questions.
3	action	continues
2	line	Player	Right... and what kind of questions are you referring to?
2	line	Wizard Persten	Well, that's the thing. It's different for everyone! Why do trees grow from stumps substantially faster than from seeds? Where do meteorites come from? Why do we have to hold our arms out to teleport successfully?
2	line	Player	I don't know. What are the answers?
2	line	Wizard Persten	I don't know either!
2	line	Player	So you're in Al Kharid to work out how trees grow?
2	line	Wizard Persten	No, silly! I came here to buy something.
2	line	Player	Something?
2	cond	If the player does not have 10 Runecraft:
3	line	Wizard Persten	That's right! Something! Tell me, what do you know of runecrafting?
3	line	Player	Not a lot really.
3	line	Wizard Persten	A shame. Unfortunately, this something requires some understanding in that area.
3	box	You do not meet all of the requirements to start the Temple of the Eye quest.
3	action	end
2	line	Wizard Persten	That's right! Something! Tell me, what do you know of the Abyss?
2	cond	If the player has not completed Enter the Abyss:
3	line	Player	Not a lot really.
3	line	Wizard Persten	A shame. Unfortunately, this something requires somewhat of an abyssal understanding.
3	box	You do not meet all of the requirements to start the Temple of the Eye quest.
3	action	end
2	line	Player	The Abyss? I know all about the Abyss.
2	line	Wizard Persten	Really? It's quite unusual for an adventurer like yourself to have knowledge in that area.
2	line	Player	Well I recently helped a group of Zamorakian wizards gain access to the Rune Essence Mine. In return, they gave me access to the Abyss.
2	line	Wizard Persten	Zamorakian wizards? You do realise that the Z.M.I. are enemies to the Order of Wizards, right?
2	line	Player	Maybe I shouldn't have mentioned that...
2	line	Wizard Persten	Oh, don't worry about it. The Order of Wizards may be a Saradominist group, but I've never personally had much time for gods. I prefer knowledge to religion.
2	line	Wizard Persten	Still, it's maybe best you don't tell anyone else. I can't imagine my fellow wizards will be happy to know that you gave away details on their secret mine.
2	line	Wizard Persten	Enough about them though. You've just shared quite the revelation with me! Is it really true that the Z.M.I. have found a way to access the Abyss?
2	line	Player	That's right.
2	line	Wizard Persten	Well in that case, I think you might be the perfect person to aid me in a little task.
2	cond	If the player has completed One Small Favour:
3	line	Player	A little task? This sounds like the time someone asked me for one small favour. I'm not sure if I'm ready for that again.
3	line	Wizard Persten	Oh, don't be silly! This will be fun!
3	line	Player	Alright, what kind of task is it?
2	cond	If the player has not completed One Small Favour:
3	line	Player	What kind of task?
2	line	Wizard Persten	Well I can't go telling you that until you agree, can I? Wouldn't want you sharing my secrets.
2	line	Player	You're not giving me much to go on here.
2	line	Wizard Persten	There'll be quite the reward for you at the end!
2	option	Yes.
3	action	below
2	option	No.
3	line	Player	I'd rather not get involved.
3	line	Wizard Persten	That's a shame. Well, you just let me know if you reconsider.
3	action	end
1	option	See you around.
2	line	Player	See you around.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Wizard Persten after declining to start the quest
1	line	Wizard Persten	Hello again! Have you changed your mind about helping me with that little task?
1	option	Yes.
2	line	Player	Alright, what do you need from me?
2	line	Wizard Persten	You'll help? Great! Well first, a question for you: you say the Z.M.I. have gained access to the Abyss? By any chance, are they using it to gain quick access to the runic altars for runecrafting purposes?
2	line	Player	Yes, but how did you...
2	line	Wizard Persten	I knew it! I've been wondering for some time how they've been creating so many runes. I'd never considered that they'd somehow gained access to the Abyss, but I now realise it was the obvious explanation.
2	line	Player	So is that what you're after? You want access to the Abyss as well?
2	line	Wizard Persten	Well, yes, but actually, no. It seems we've jumped ahead a bit. Let's go back to why I'm here.
2	line	Player	The 'something' you bought?
2	line	Wizard Persten	The 'something' I bought! Here, take a look.
2	box	Persten shows you an amulet.
2	line	Wizard Persten	A foolish archaeologist by the name of Asgarnia Smith recently found this washed up near the Ruins of Uzer. Despite his apparent archaeological credentials, he dismissed it as junk.
2	line	Wizard Persten	Luckily, I was able to buy it from him before he disposed of it. Can you believe he thought the 100 coins I paid was too much? If only he knew the true value of something like this...
2	line	Player	Why is it so valuable?
2	line	Wizard Persten	You see that eye on it? That is the symbol of both the Order of Wizards and our home, the Wizards' Tower. Thing is, that's only the start.
2	line	Wizard Persten	From what I can tell, this amulet is thousands of years old, but our order was only formed at the dawn of the Fifth Age. That wasn't even two hundred years ago!
2	line	Player	But how...
2	line	Wizard Persten	Hang on! I'm not done yet. I also inspected the amulet for magical energies and found something fascinating! I recognised two distinct magical signatures.
2	line	Wizard Persten	The first is the same magic found in rune essence. That's already pretty exciting, but it's the second that will blow your mind!
2	line	Player	What was it?
2	line	Wizard Persten	I'm getting to that! My, you do like interrupting, don't you? Don't worry, I understand. I get quite excited about these things as well!
2	line	Wizard Persten	Anyway, here's the big reveal for you: the second signature was energy from the Abyss!
2	line	Player	So you have an amulet with the symbol of your order on it, but it predates your order by thousands of years?
2	line	Player	It also turned up miles from where your order is based, and is filled with energy from a dimension that until recently, no one had even been to?
2	line	Wizard Persten	Now you see why this is so exciting!
2	line	Player	So what do you need from me?
2	line	Wizard Persten	I need to find out where this amulet came from. It should be possible to trace it using the abyssal energy it still contains.
2	line	Wizard Persten	This is where you ask 'What's the catch?'
2	line	Player	*sigh* What's the catch?
2	line	Wizard Persten	I'm glad you asked, {player}! Unfortunately, the spell needed to trace the amulet will only work properly from inside the Abyss.
2	line	Player	Oh I see where this is going. You don't have access to the Abyss, but I do.
2	line	Wizard Persten	Precisely! While I don't care about the religious squabbling between the Z.M.I. and my order, I still can't see them wanting to work with me any time soon.
2	line	Player	So I need to take this amulet to the Abyss and work out where it came from?
2	line	Wizard Persten	Correct! I imagine you'll need the help of your Z.M.I. friends.
2	line	Wizard Persten	Just maybe don't tell them who gave it to you.
2	line	Player	I'll visit the Mage of Zamorak in Varrock. He should be able to help me.
2	line	Wizard Persten	Return to me once you are done. Oh, and don't forget the amulet!
2	cond	If the player has inventory space:
3	box	Persten hands you the amulet.
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player does not have inventory space:
3	box	Persten tries to hand you the amulet, but you don't have enough room to take it.
3	action	end
1	option	No.
2	line	Player	I'd rather not get involved.
2	line	Wizard Persten	That's a shame. Well, you just let me know if you reconsider.
2	action	end
