0	section	Help from Some Wizards
0	section	Talking to Wizard Persten
1	line	Wizard Persten	Hello again! Any luck with that amulet?
1	line	Player	Yes! I have an incantation that could lead us to wherever it came from.
1	line	Wizard Persten	Brilliant! Let's have a look.
1	box	You show the incantation to Persten and she quickly makes a copy for herself.
1	line	Wizard Persten	Oh, fascinating! Hmm... But that would mean...
1	line	Player	That would mean what?
1	line	Wizard Persten	Shhh! I'm thinking.
1	line	Player	...
1	line	Wizard Persten	Yes... Two... no three more! Silly me! Counted myself didn't I.
1	line	Wizard Persten	Well it should be fine. I can't see them saying no. After all, it's their symbol as well...
1	line	Player	What are you on about?
1	line	Wizard Persten	Oh yes, you're here! Brilliant! You'll be pleased to know that I've worked out what we must do next.
1	line	Player	And that is?
1	line	Wizard Persten	Patience, young adventurer. Before we get to that, let me share with you my theory on where this amulet came from.
1	line	Wizard Persten	While you were gone, I was thinking about why the amulet would have magical energy from both rune essence and the Abyss. All of a sudden, it hit me!
1	line	Player	Ouch?
1	line	Wizard Persten	Quite the opposite! The source of this amulet must be an ancient teleportation matrix to the runic altars, just like the one the Z.M.I. have in the Abyss!
1	line	Wizard Persten	This is good news, in case you were wondering! Access to a teleportation matrix like that will be life changing when it comes to my work!
1	line	Wizard Persten	Of course, the rest of my order will be very happy as well. It'll completely remove the advantage the Z.M.I. currently have. Now there's a balance that Guthix himself would love!
1	cond	If the player has the amulet:
2	line	Wizard Persten	Ah, but this talk of the Z.M.I. has reminded me of something. Could I have that amulet back?
2	line	Player	Here you go.
2	box	You give the amulet back to Persten.
2	action	continues
1	cond	If the player lost the amulet:
2	line	Wizard Persten	Ah, but this talk of the Z.M.I. has reminded me of something. You lost that amulet didn't you?
2	line	Player	Maybe...
2	line	Wizard Persten	Don't worry, I found it for you. I'll keep hold of it for now.
2	action	continues
1	line	Wizard Persten	Now, just give me a moment...
1	box	Persten casts a spell on the amulet.
1	line	Wizard Persten	Ah, yes. Well, that's not surprising.
1	line	Player	What is it?
1	line	Wizard Persten	Your Z.M.I. friends cast a transmission spell on the amulet. Had we taken it with us, it would have transmitted all sorts of information back to them about the origin.
1	line	Wizard Persten	It's not a problem. I suspected they might do something like this. The good news is that this means they have no intention of using that incantation themselves.
1	line	Wizard Persten	Again, as expected. They prefer to lurk in the shadows. To be honest, I totally understand. I've been known to do the same from time to time.
1	line	Wizard Persten	Anyway, I've modified their spell to send false information to them. They'll be none the wiser.
1	line	Player	I thought you didn't care about religion? Why don't you want the Z.M.I. getting that information?
1	line	Wizard Persten	Oh, my friend, you misunderstand. I have no issues with the Z.M.I. having the information, but I don't want them getting it before I've even had a chance to determine what it is!
1	line	Player	I see. So what now?
1	line	Wizard Persten	Yes, back to business! The incantation is quite complex, so we will need the help of three other wizards to perform it. I'm afraid I'm not including you in that, although you are very talented!
1	line	Player	Thanks, I think... so where do we get these other wizards?
1	line	Wizard Persten	From the Wizards' Tower of course! My fellow wizards won't be able to resist getting their hands on a teleportation matrix, especially one that may be connected to the history of our order!
1	line	Wizard Persten	Now, you head to the Wizards' Tower and show that incantation to Sedridor. I have a couple of things to prepare first, but I will join you there soon.
1	line	Wizard Persten	Oh, and whatever you do, don't mention the Z.M.I. while you're there.
1	line	Player	Alright, I'll see you soon.
1	line	Wizard Persten	Hey, if you want, I can teleport you to the Wizards' Tower. Consider it a one-time gift from me.
1	select	Teleport to the Wizards' Tower? You can only use this teleport once.
1	option	Yes.
1	option	No.
2	line	Player	I think I'll walk.
2	line	Wizard Persten	Well let me know if you change your mind.
2	action	end
