1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Tamara again after returning from the Water Altar
1	line	Player	I have another cell. Do you want me to power up the barrier again?
1	line	Apprentice Tamara	That's right! If my theory is correct, it should produce an even stronger barrier!
1	action	end
0	section	Placing the medium cell
1	line	Player	Look! The barrier changed!
1	line	Apprentice Tamara	Just as I thought! We can create better barriers by using stronger cells!
1	line	Apprentice Tamara	Now, let's charge the guardian with those stones you created and close this rift!
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Tamara again
1	line	Apprentice Tamara	Let's charge the guardian with those stones you created and close this rift!
1	action	end
0	section	Closing the rift
1	line	The Great Guardian	Humans, I now have the power to close the rift. Brace yourselves!
1	line	The Great Guardian	We are safe, for now.
1	line	Apprentice Tamara	What was all that? What happened?
1	line	The Great Guardian	That was a rift into an area of the Abyss known as the Scar.
1	line	Apprentice Cordelia	The Scar? But I thought this was meant to be a teleportation matrix.
1	line	The Great Guardian	You are mistaken. While it is true that teleportation magic is strong here, that is only a side effect of this temple's history.
1	line	Apprentice Felix	What history?
1	line	The Great Guardian	This temple was built to house a powerful artefact. Many sought to claim this artefact for themselves, including servants of the Fallen Empire.
1	line	The Great Guardian	In their attempt to claim the artefact, they used magic they did not understand. The rift to the Scar was created as a result.
1	line	Player	This artefact... you mean the Eye?
1	line	The Great Guardian	You are correct. The Eye was removed after the battle, but not before the Justiciar of the Lion used it to seal the rift once more.
1	line	The Great Guardian	She then created us, the Guardians of the Rift, to protect this place in the event the rift was ever reopened.
1	line	Apprentice Felix	And we reopened it.
1	line	Apprentice Cordelia	But it's been sealed again now! The danger is gone.
1	line	The Great Guardian	Incorrect. Without the power of the Eye, we have no way to seal the rift permanently. It will soon reopen once more. You should leave before that happens.
1	line	Apprentice Tamara	No. This was our mistake. I'm staying to help fix it.
1	line	Apprentice Felix	Me too!
1	line	Apprentice Cordelia	Well if you two are staying, I guess I will as well.
1	line	The Great Guardian	Your support will be invaluable.
1	line	Apprentice Tamara	{player}, could you go back to the Wizards' Tower and let Sedridor know what happened here?
1	line	Player	Alright, if you're absolutely sure about this.
1	line	Apprentice Felix	What about Persten? We have to help her.
1	line	The Great Guardian	No part of the Abyss is more dangerous than the Scar. Your friend will have already been consumed.
1	line	The Great Guardian	Now, the power of the Abyss grows. The rift will soon reopen once more. Those of you staying should prepare yourselves.
1	line	Player	Then I guess I'd better go and see Sedridor. Good luck.
1	action	Sedridor cutscene continues below.
0	section	Talking to Sedridor after leaving the temple, or using the portal
1	action	Sedridor cutscene continues below.
0	section	Sedridor cutscene
1	line	Player	Sedridor! It all went wrong!
1	line	Archmage Sedridor	What do you mean? Was there no teleportation matrix?
1	line	Player	Kind of, but not really. The portal took us to the Temple of the Eye, an ancient Saradominist temple built to house a powerful artefact.
1	line	Player	Long ago, a rift to the Abyss was created in the temple, but it was sealed. At least it was, until Persten accidently opened it again...
1	line	Player	She was sucked into the Abyss, and all these abyssal creatures came out!
1	line	Archmage Sedridor	Abyssal creatures? We have to get in there and stop this!
1	line	Player	It's okay again, for now. Some rune guardians called the Guardians of the Rift were built to protect the temple from the Abyss. They helped us close the rift again, but they say it will soon reopen.
1	line	Archmage Sedridor	This is a disaster! I knew that teleportation matrix was too good to be true. I should have stopped this, but I was blinded by my own desires for that matrix!
1	line	Archmage Sedridor	What of Traiborn's apprentices?
1	line	Player	They're safe. They chose to stay and help the Guardians of the Rift keep the rift closed.
1	line	Archmage Sedridor	Then I will ensure they have all the help they need. I will also begin researching this rift at once. Maybe we can still find a way to close it permanently.
1	line	Archmage Sedridor	In the meantime, I suggest you do what you can to help them as well. After all, this is partially your doing.
1	line	Player	I know. I'll help wherever I'm needed.
1	line	Archmage Sedridor	Thank you, {player}. I appreciate that you did not mean for things to go this way. You should have this. It belonged to Persten. I don't want to think about where she got it.
1	box	Sedridor shows you a pouch.
1	line	Player	Do you think she's still alive?
1	line	Archmage Sedridor	Sadly, that seems unlikely. Still, if anyone can survive the Abyss, it's her.
1	line	Archmage Sedridor	Now, we'd better get to work.
0	section	Post-quest dialogue
0	section	Archmage Sedridor
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	line	Archmage Sedridor	Hello again, {player}. What can I do for you?
1	option	Can you teleport me to the Rune Essence Mine?
1	option	How are things at the Temple of the Eye?
2	line	Player	How are things at the Temple of the Eye?
2	line	Archmage Sedridor	Between the Guardians of the Rift and ourselves, we are managing to keep the Abyss at bay.
2	line	Archmage Sedridor	However, despite all our research, we are no closer to working out how to close the rift permanently.
2	line	Archmage Sedridor	Gaining a better understanding of the artefact that was once there is key, but we have found little mention of this 'Eye'.
2	line	Archmage Sedridor	I'm sure the wizards of the first tower had plenty of research on it. After all, they knew enough about it to use its symbol as the symbol for our order.
2	line	Archmage Sedridor	All that knowledge lost because of those accursed Zamorakians!
2	line	Archmage Sedridor	Anyway, if you wish to help defend the temple, just head through the portal.
2	action	other
1	option	Who else knows the teleport to the Rune Essence Mine?
1	option	Could you tell me about the old Wizards' Tower?
2	line	Player	Could you tell me about the old Wizards' Tower?
2	line	Archmage Sedridor	Of course. The first Wizards' Tower was built at the same time the Order of Wizards was founded. It was at the dawn of the Fifth Age, when the secrets of runecrafting were rediscovered.
2	line	Archmage Sedridor	For years, the tower was a hub of magical research. Wizards of all races and religions were welcomed into our order.
2	line	Archmage Sedridor	Alas, that openness is what ultimately led to disaster. The wizards who served Zamorak, the evil god of chaos, tried to claim our magical discoveries in his name.
2	line	Archmage Sedridor	They failed, but in retaliation, they burnt the entire tower to the ground. Years of work was destroyed.
2	line	Archmage Sedridor	The tower was soon rebuilt of course, but even now we are still trying to regain knowledge that was lost.
2	line	Archmage Sedridor	That's why I spend my time down here, in fact. This basement is all that is left of the old tower, and I believe there are still some secrets to discover here.
2	line	Archmage Sedridor	Of course, one secret I am no longer looking for is the teleportation incantation to the Rune Essence Mine. We have you to thank for that.
2	cond	If the player did not speak to the Mage of Zamorak about the abyssal incantation post-quest:
3	action	other
2	cond	If the player spoke to the Mage of Zamorak about the abyssal incantation post-quest:
3	line	Player	I've heard a different take on how the tower burnt down. Something about a ritual gone wrong?
3	line	Archmage Sedridor	Nothing more than Zamorakian hearsay! They burnt the tower down and are now too cowardly to even admit it!
3	line	Player	Fair enough.
3	action	other
1	option	Nothing thanks, I'm just looking around.
0	section	Mage of Zamorak
1	line	Mage of Zamorak	Ah, you again. What do you want?
1	option	About that incantation your initiate gave me...
2	line	Player	About that incantation your initiate gave me...
2	line	Mage of Zamorak	Ah yes, the one to trace that amulet. Don't think I didn't notice that you modified the transmission spell I put on it. Next time you need help, we might not be so willing.
2	line	Player	Well maybe you should have asked first! Besides, you wouldn't have got anything useful out of it. In tracing that amulet, we accidently managed to open an uncontrollable rift to the Abyss.
2	line	Mage of Zamorak	And does this 'we' include the Order of Wizards?
2	line	Player	Maybe...
2	line	Mage of Zamorak	I knew it! It's just like them to play with magic they don't understand. First they burnt down the Wizards' Tower, now they're opening uncontrollable abyssal rifts!
2	line	Mage of Zamorak	Perhaps the fools should leave the dangerous magic to us next time!
2	line	Player	Oh, that reminds me. That incantation didn't appear to be written on parchment. What was it?
2	line	Mage of Zamorak	Hmm... probably the flesh of an abyssal creature. Why do you ask?
2	line	Player	Oh, I just thought it might be human flesh. I'm relieved it wasn't!
2	line	Mage of Zamorak	You've been spending too much time with your friends in the Order of Wizards! I know that we Zamorakians have a bad reputation, but do you really think we'd be so barbaric?
2	action	other
1	option	Can you tell me more about the Abyss?
1	option	Can you tell me more about your group?
